hem they want security  they want economic economic prosperity  and if you look at the united arab  emirates and you look at israel they're  both technology powerhouses financial  powerhouses  and most importantly security  powerhouses so this really is a great  alignment and again president  trump uh built trust after the last  administration both parties had  uh felt uh down on their relationship  with america they felt very very  betrayed after  uh the iran deal which sent 150 billion  dollars to iran and they  used that money to fund a lot of the  proxies that were destabilizing the  region  but president trump has rebuilt that  trust he's brought them closer together  and he's aligned them around a common  vision that could be good and i will say  this too you know somebody said to me  very early on when i got this  assignment they said you don't lose  money betting against success in the  middle east but  i also say you can lose a lot of money  betting against trump and  president trump took on this challenge  he wasn't afraid to fail  he tried doing it in an unconventional  way and by doing it he's achieved a  truly historic result well i want to uh  i want to ask you another question about  this and first i want to  let you listen to prime minister  netanyahu and his comments late this  afternoon sure  this is the greatest advancements toward  peace between israel  and the arab world in the last 26 years  this is a future of peace  a future of security and the future of  prosperity  when did the prime minister finally  agree to hold off on annexation  and do you have a sense of how long this  pause is going to be  so we've been speaking about what  annexation would look like for the last  six months you know you know the prime  minister  really is a historic leader he's a  visionary he's  uh he he was able to agree to a  two-state solution  with the palestinians on the basis of  president trump's vision for peace and  to  have the first time we ever had a map  forward so we were talking about how we  could implement this plan  because by implementing the plan we'd  actually be saving the two-state  solution  not destroying it which would be a  massive change so we've been talking  about it for a bunch of  uh months and then obviously over the  last six weeks the notion  of a normalization in lieu of a uh of  applying israeli sovereignty came  up and uh prime minister netanyahu did  the calculus and saw that  this was much more in the interests of  israel in the short medium and long term  and  that's what great leaders do they put  the politics aside and they make the  right decisions  that strengthen their countries and keep  their people safe all right i want to  turn to the election  you're deeply involved you were last  time you're this time  uh you just heard our new fox news poll  uh with  uh vice president former vice president  biden leading by seven points in that  poll  but in the job performance uh the  president is at 44  disapproved 54 percent uh and and in who  is trusted to do a better job uh on  different issues  uh the president is up three on the  economy but he is losing to vice  president biden on a number of  key issues where do you see this race  right now so  we've spoken about the methodology of  the fox polls and  we saw in the last election out of 120  polls conducted in michigan wisconsin  and pennsylvania  between labor day and the election out  of 120 only one showed  president trump ahead so uh this these  polls are based off of flawed  methodology  uh our polls basically show that the  president is leading in a lot of the  states that he won last time  and we were just in ohio and our team we  won the president won ohio by eight and  a half points  he believes he's going to win by more  this time and if you go state by state  and you look at real voter turnout  models  you look at the enthusiasm we're seeing  very very encouraging signs on the  ground and  we think the people of this country love  what president trump's doing and they  want to see him back  in the in office for four more years so  that he can  continue to rebuild the economy and  finish the job that he started just to  be clear when you say flawed you'd like  to see likely voters not registered  voters you'd like to see a small the  sample that matches how you see the  election shaping up but if you look at  the real clear politics average  uh joe biden is up seven and a half  points it's an average of recent polls  across the board  and the average of battlegrounds you can  see biden with the lead  i get that you don't like polls at this  point and you like them to be likely  no but what i would just say is look on  election day last year everyone thought  it was going to be a landslide i was  looking at our data and our show that  trump  data showed that trump was going to win  the landslide a lot of those polls are  using a 24  republican turnout model but in 2018 and  2016  it was 33 so i don't know why the  companies are spending money  on these polls because it's not  scientific and it's not indicative of  what's actually going to happen but  that's another story yeah well we can  talk about poll  methodology and as we get closer we'll  get a different  mindset as we look at those i want to  ask you the president addressed these  questions about  the post office and about funding the  post office spent a lot of time in that  briefing  the critics are saying that after his  interview with maria bartoromo today  that he's essentially brazenly  attempting to  what they say is steal the election by  invalidating vote by mail ballots  or that he's deliberately damaging the  post office to somehow  change the election address that from  that charge  that the critics are giving yeah one of  the presidents trump's many skills is  that he gets his critics to go crazy on  all types of things and end up making  his point  all president trump's been trying to say  is that uh there are some states that  have been doing mail-in ballots in  different forms whether it's absentee  ballot  and they do it appropriately if you're  trying to rush a whole system all the  recent examples are showing  that it just doesn't work it's not  seamless it's like saying we're trusting  the post office to be the most efficient  arbiter of our democracy  i don't think anyone thinks that that's  the case so president trump is trying to  bring  attention to an issue and it is a big  issue we saw that in new york we've seen  that in various states  and president trump just wants a fair  and well-run election and he's working  hard to make sure that that happens  all right another thing that's setting  off the critics is you and ivanka  meeting with kanye west in colorado  you said you've been friends however he  is running for president there are  charges that  uh that this is a coordinated plan to  somehow siphon black votes away from  from joe biden how do you respond to  that yeah look  unlike others i'm able to keep  friendships across the aisle and  and kanye's been a friend for 10 years  he's a very very special person  he's a very successful music artist he's  a very successful designer he's been  very successful a lot of the things he's  done  we were together in the same spot kanye  sent me a book  about a month ago called powernomics by  dr claude anderson i read the book it  was absolutely phenomenal it actually  incorporated a lot of the things that  president trump has been doing and it's  something i've distributed more copies  to my domestic policy team because i  think there's a lot of inspiration we  can get from it  for president trump's second term agenda  so we were more talking about ideas and  uh again friendships uh should trump  politics and uh  that's what's most do you know that are  the charges that republican operatives  are trying to help him get on these  ballots  is that true do you know that again we  we did not discuss his uh his campaign  and  uh and i'm what he's up to i read things  in the press but  i have not discussed that directly with  him okay and you don't know that that's  happening  uh look like i've said i've learned in  five years of doing this now that  uh just because something's said in the  media doesn't mean it's true so i'd like  to investigate the facts look at the  real data  and unless i feel like something's  verified i tend not to  assume that it's it's gospel all right  two more things really quickly who's  really in charge of the campaign  there's some who think that you are  still the de facto campaign manager  uh president trump has always been in  charge of the campaign and he always  will be in charge of the campaign and  my job is to help him make sure that he  has good options for people good people  around him  and people who can execute and right now  we have over 1500 people in the field  we've got over a million and a half  volunteers  we've got a tremendous organization the  online fundraising has been tremendous  and so president trump has a very very  strong operation but that's because of  his leadership  and his vision he sets the message he  sets the tone he decides where he wants  to go  and he's got a lot of people like myself  who help him execute that  you know uh very last thing you said he  likes to stir up his critics  at that press briefing he seemed to give  credence to a newsweek  op-ed that questioned the eligibility of  kamala harris  uh being able to run for vice president  why why do that i'll be honest brett  i've been out here waiting to do your  show so i haven't seen that i haven't  seen the op-ed so  i'll reserve judgment on that until i  know more about it okay  she was born in oakland california the  indian and jamaican immigrants  on california soil she's natural born  citizen anyway  if you see this election are you losing  right now  or do you see that you have to make up  ground  before november 3rd how do you see it  playing out over 